\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl\cf1\b0\f1\fs22 There's a book called \lquote The Chronicles of Corporal Crag\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote But as we marched 'cross the rolling plains and meadows, encounters with roaming monsters grew more frequent. 'Twas not long ere we met with the most dreaded of them all\emdash the dragon.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Clad head-to-toe in scales hard as stone, neither sword nor spear could make but the slightest scratch in the beast's hide. It seemed certain to slay us to a man...\par
\par
\par
\lquote I swung my blade in wild desperation. Somehow, a blow connected and sent the great lizard reeling. We fled without a moment's hesitation, fearing that it might soon regain its composure.\par
\par
\par
\lquote To this day, I know not why my attack had the effect it did, but I and every one of my men owe our lives to this miraculous quirk of fate.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2033\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a scrap of paper hidden in between two books. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote There's nothing I love more than the longing looks of those slum-dwellers who pass beneath my balcony and gawk at my treasure chest with their hungry eyes.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The envy of the unwashed masses is well founded, for the chest holds my greatest treasures. But I rest easy in the knowledge that it remains completely inaccessible.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Just as I did yesterday and today, tomorrow I shall bask in the covetous glance of the rats scurrying below! Ahahahaha!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote A Brief History of Heliodor\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Situated atop rocky cliffs, Heliodor was never blessed with fertile soil or bounteous rains. Farmers could never reap a plentiful harvest from its earth, which all agreed was barren.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But one day, in search of a land to call their own, two brothers came to these unwelcoming wilds, and began a daring attempt to reclaim them from nature.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Many sneered at their seeming folly, but the brothers paid them no heed, and toiled on. A grand irrigation system soon saw the soil brought to life, and their first yield of crops exceeded all expectations.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Their deeds united the farming families around them, and a new, united realm soon sprang up from the transformed land with the two brothers as its kings. Thus was born the nation of Heliodor.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2033\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote A Spotter's Guide to Monsters\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Intrepid Adventurer! If this book should impress upon you one thing before you set out on your quest to see the world, let it be this:\par
\par
\par
\lquote The monsters that roam the land at night are far more fearsome than those that appear during the day!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Heed these words well, adventurer, and go abroad in the evening only if you are prepared to meet the dangers that await you.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2614\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote A Blacksmith Abroad, by Haul Bellows\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote My name is Haul, but most know me as the Wandering Blacksmith. Throughout my travels, I have heard many a rumour of a particularly wondrous little forge.\par
\par
\par
\lquote It is said that one can throw any number of odds and ends into it, and in doing so produce countless fabulous creations. But surely these stories are too fanciful to take at face value?\par
\par
\par
\lquote Yet should there be some truth to them, a wise adventurer would do well to hold on to whatever oddments they find on their travels\emdash who knows what they might be turned into!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a magazine entitled \lquote Down and Out in Downtown Heliodor\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote In last month's issue, we shed some light on the lesser-known highlights of Heliodor's historic city centre. This month, we'd like to take a moment to talk about the city's diverse downtown district.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The land this quarter occupies once served as a defensive trench, but with the town's population growing by the day, new arrivals had no choice but to make their homes in this ditch beyond the walls.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Soon, the bustling shanty town had attracted a whole host of colourful characters, and came to be known as a place of great risk, but also of great opportunity.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Downtown Heliodor's struggle with crime is no secret, but for some thrill seekers, it offers an excitement found nowhere else. Do you dare take a walk on the wild side?\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Lurid Allure of the Dingy Dungeons\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Far below the basements and storerooms of Heliodor Castle, deep within its very bowels, lie the dungeons that house the most heinous and hardened criminals in the kingdom.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Many who have been locked away in these cold, dank cells have not lived to see the outside world again.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Those whose crimes are deemed truly unforgivable are thrown into the deepest cells of all, from which it is said to be all but impossible to escape. A death sentence in all but name...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Take care to stay on the right side of the law, dear reader, lest you too be locked up, and the key thrown away forever.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Soldier and the Strategist \endash  A Tale of Two Heroes\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
It appears to be a detailed biography of the two great knights who protect the kingdom of Heliodor.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4646\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Soldier and the Strategist \endash  A Tale of Two Heroes\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote No matter how ferocious an assault the monsters may launch against Heliodor, this great kingdom shall not fall, for two heroic figures will stand in the path of any attacker.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The first is Sir Hendrik, a warrior without equal. Countless times has he ridden his colossal black steed Obsidian fearlessly into the heart of an oncoming assault, scattering the enemy like so many leaves.\par
\par
\par
\lquote He is chivalrous to a fault, and considered by many to be the greatest swordsman in the world\emdash even the vilest, most towering troll dare not stand its ground when faced with his whirling greatsword.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The second half of this gallant duo is the shrewd and ingenious Sir Jasper. Regarded as the sharpest military mind of the age, he has led heavily outnumbered forces to glorious victory again and again.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Though as a swordsman he may be no match for Sir Hendrik, his ability to analyse any battlefield and quickly arrive at the ideal strategy for the situation at hand is unrivalled.\par
\par
\par
\lquote With these two great men\emdash the Swordsman and the Strategist\emdash to protect it, Heliodor need fear no foe.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote National Treasures, No. 106 \endash  The Shield of Heliodor\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Our tale begins with the first king of Zwaardsrust and his retinue resting at a Heliodorian inn after many days' hard travel.\par
\par
\par
\lquote A great black dragon heard the news and, deciding that this would be the perfect opportunity to slay the king of Zwaardsrust, launched a blazing assault on the city.\par
\par
\par
\lquote As the citizens of Heliodor flew into a panic, a lone knight stood before them with his arms outstretched, doing all that he could to protect them from the foul lizard's wrath.\par
\par
\par
\lquote So greatly moved was the king of Zwaardsrust by the knight's selfless bravery that he presented him with a fine shield in the shape of a great black dragon scale.\par
\par
\par
\lquote To this day, that fabulous treasure can be found in Heliodor. The King may choose to present it to any knight he deems worthy of the honour and responsibility of the role it represents: first knight of the realm.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4356\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Drustan's Armour\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote The mermaid princess led King Drustan deep beneath the waves to an undersea realm, where the citizens were engaged in a contest of strength, wrestling one another in order to be recognised as the strongest.\par
\par
\par
\lquote\ldblquote If you can defeat my father,\rdblquote  the princess told him, \ldblquote he will grant you my hand in marriage...\rdblquote\par
\par
\par
\lquote And thus the two kings fought. But so perfectly were these warriors matched that though they wrestled for seven days and seven nights, neither could claim victory.\par
\par
\par
\lquote So awestruck was the king of the ocean at the warrior king's might that he offered him not only his daughter's hand in marriage, but also one of the great treasures of his realm.\par
\par
\par
\lquote From this treasure\emdash a lustrous, scarlet scale as strong as steel and as light as silk\emdash the warrior king forged a beautiful suit of crimson armour.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But he could not wed the princess, for he was a man of his word, and had not defeated her father. He turned his back on his beloved and, to her dismay, left the undersea kingdom, never to return...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2033\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a massive, boring-looking book here entitled \lquote Proceedings of the 36th Annual Conference on Heliodorian Development\rquote . Eleven heaves it down to take a closer look...\par
\par
\par
The margins are filled with mouth-watering drawings of cakes and tarts! Each picture is accompanied by detailed notes describing the fabulous flavours of these delectable desserts!\par
\par
\par
\lquote\emdash  Scrumptious Strawberry Mousse \emdash\par
\par
The exquisite pairing of fluffy, delicate mousse with ever-so-slightly sour strawberries is a match made in heaven!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1452\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an old, time-worn diary covered in a child's scribblings. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
With faltering lines, someone has drawn what appears to be a pair of...matchsticks? One of them has a beard, the other is wearing a ribbon.\par
\par
\par
Beneath the illustration it says \lquote my dady an me\rquote . \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote King Carnelian: Behind the Throne\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Having seen several generations of his line, I can say with some certainty that King Carnelian is a rare breed of monarch, possessed of all the qualities required in a truly great leader.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Both loved and feared by the populace, he is like a father to them\emdash kind yet stern, firm yet fair. Not since the days of the great kings of old has our nation been so blessed.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Though his face may have grown hard and lined since the terrible events that took place those few short years ago, some might say that this has added a certain...depth that improves him yet further.\par
\par
\par
\lquote To have so resolutely overcome such grief and yet still led his nation boldly onward is surely a sign that Carnelian is a king among kings.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2614\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Erdrean Geographic\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Of the many nations, both large and small, that make up Erdrea, there are five\emdash the so-called \ldblquote Great Five\rdblquote\emdash that stand above all others in the eyes of the world.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Ancient and honourable Dundrasil, steadfast and stony Heliodor, Gallopolis with its noble desert knights, Sniflheim with its snow-capped towers and last but not least, Zwaardsrust, carpeted in flowers.\par
\par
\par
\lquote These five nations guide the world, meeting every few years at the great conference known as the Colloquy of Kings in order to steer the course of Erdrean affairs in a direction agreeable to all.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient book here. The binding is almost completely worn through, and Eleven can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Drustaniad: Secrets of ye Heart\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\par
\par
He tries to read a page or two, but something tells him he's not quite ready yet...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2323\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient book here. The binding is almost completely worn through, and Eleven can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Drustaniad: Secrets of ye Heart\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Though I have written much concerning the techniques by which a warrior might perfect his craft, these techniques are all as naught if he be not sound of heart and mind.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Come what may, a calm, clear spirit shalt see thee through. 'Tis in ye heart that victory is won.\rquote\par
\par
\par
Eleven has uncovered one of Drustan's teachings, and learned the Secret of the Spirit. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1452\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an old, time-worn diary covered in a child's scribblings. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
With faltering lines, someone has drawn what appears to be a pair of...matchsticks? One of them has a beard, the other is wearing a ribbon.\par
\par
\par
Beneath the illustration it says \lquote my dady an me\rquote . \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote National Treasures, No. 106 \endash  The Shield of Heliodor\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Our tale begins with the first king of Zwaardsrust and his retinue resting at a Heliodorian inn after many days' hard travel.\par
\par
\par
\lquote A great black dragon heard the news and, deciding that this would be the perfect opportunity to slay the king of Zwaardsrust, launched a blazing assault on the city.\par
\par
\par
\lquote As the citizens of Heliodor flew into a panic, a lone knight stood before them with his arms outstretched, doing all that he could to protect them from the foul lizard's wrath.\par
\par
\par
\lquote So greatly moved was the king of Zwaardsrust by the knight's selfless bravery that he presented him with a fine shield in the shape of a great black dragon scale.\par
\par
\par
\lquote To this day, that fabulous treasure can be found in Heliodor. The King may choose to present it any knight he deems worthy of the honour and responsibility of the role it represents: first knight of the realm.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Deadly Denizens of the Celestial Sands\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote In this volume, I shall describe a select few among the countless ferocious monsters that infest the harsh, unforgiving dunes of the Celestial Sands.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The Spitzfire: A naturally nocturnal beast that spends the daylight hours asleep (thankfully). Should you ever be unfortunate enough to happen upon one, take good care not to wake it.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The Slayer of the Sands: An enormous arthropod that has slain too many brave Gallopolitan knights to count. It is thought mainly to prowl the very centre of the Celestial Sands.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The Cactolotl: Swimming through the sands as if they were water, it attracts its prey with a scent like that of cactus flowers. Few have seen it and lived, but all who have agree that it is the true lord of the desert.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a distinctly old-fashioned looking history book entitled \lquote The Guardians of the Star\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Whatever could have led people to brave the harsh desert heat and make their homes in the arid land of Gallopolis? To answer this question, we must go back to the very founding of the nation.\par
\par
\par
\lquote What records remain of the gallant men who first settled here refer to them as the Guardians of the Star. It is safe to surmise that their descendants went on to become the current royal family of Gallopolis.\par
\par
\par
\lquote We cannot know for sure how these first men came to earn such a title, but more than a few have speculated upon a link with the nation's renowned knights and the numerous checkpoints they guard...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Wanderers No More: The Gallopolitan Circus\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Our humble circus was once like many others\emdash a travelling spectacle that traversed Erdrea from one land to another.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But when our itinerant troupe finally arrived in the great kingdom of Gallopolis, the people were so warm and enthusiastic that the Sultan himself suggested we stay.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But we were wanderers at heart. We belonged on the road. With tears in our eyes, we turned down this most generous offer, and regretfully left the friendly people of the desert behind.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But when next we returned, what we saw amazed us all: the Sultan had ordered the construction of an enormous, beautiful big top in which we might ply our entertaining trade!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Each and every one of us was so moved by this grand gesture that the decision to remain was unanimous. The rest, as they say, is history!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's what appears to be a diary here. It has \lquote Prince Faris's Progress\rquote  written on the cover. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Day 21.\par
\par
My beloved Prince attended his horse-riding lessons once more today.\par
\par
\par
\lquote To see him training day in and day out to be the greatest leader he can be for the noble knights of Gallopolis fills me with hope for the magnificent future he will no doubt usher in for our realm!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Day 24.\par
\par
My beloved Prince left the palace today and went out into the streets to speak with the common people.\par
\par
\par
\lquote He seeks to study the lifestyles of his subjects first-hand\emdash what a wise and benevolent young man he is! I have no doubt he will make a great sultan some day!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient book here. The binding is almost completely worn through, and <cc> can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Drustaniad: Secrets of ye Flame\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\par
\par
<LM_Gender_cc(He,She,It)> tries to read a page or two, but something tells <LM_Gender_cc(him,her,it)> <LM_Gender_cc(he,she,it)>'s not quite ready yet...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2323\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient book here. The binding is almost completely worn through, and Eleven can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Drustaniad: Secrets of ye Flame\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\par
\par
\lquote One single word encapsulates all that I have learned of the art of offence in my long and storied career: \ldblquote fire\rdblquote .\par
\par
\par
\lquote As ye fire sweeps unbidden and unbound through ye fields, so sweep through thine enemies, striking swift and true. No defence can stand before such an onslaught.\rquote\par
\par
\par
Eleven has uncovered one of Drustan's teachings, and learned the Secret of Offence.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2614\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Power of Positivity: A Ruler's Handbook\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote We have all heard what they say: should one wish to be a great leader, one must be positive at all times\emdash and it is true!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Who would want to follow a mopey, indecisive man anywhere? Nobody, that is who! So forget all those negative thoughts and think positive!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Lie flat on your back, gaze up at the big, blue sky and feel your troubles melt away like the petty, insignificant irritations they are!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Say goodbye to the old you\emdash the negative you. There is a bright and positive future waiting for you, so step right up and take it!\rquote  \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl This book was frozen solid before, and now that the ice has melted, it's completely soaked through! The ink has run, and the writing is completely illegible...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2033\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Sun, Sea and Scandalous Swimsuits\rquote  with some young ladies in bikinis on the cover. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
It's full of photographs of perky young women in skimpy swimwear, bouncing about on the pristine white sands of a summery beach.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Hooray! Every day is summer here on Paradise Beach! It's hot, hot, hot, and right now it's time for the breaststroke grand finals!\rquote\par
\par
\par
It seems like it might have been designed to...keep lonely souls warm on cold winter nights...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh5227\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Memoirs of a Treasure Hunter: Volume IV\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote This is the diary of Sudo Nim, treasure hunter extraordinaire. In my search for the Rainbough, I had almost made my way to the city of Sniflheim, where I had heard I'd find the greatest minds in Erdrea.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But my plans changed, as plans have a way of doing. On my way, I came across a young man collapsed by the roadside, and nearly buried in heavy snow. I couldn't just leave the poor lad be\emdash I had to help him!\par
\par
\par
\lquote The poor boy was frightful sick, and delirious with fever. I could scarce make head nor tail of his twaddling, but there was one thing he kept repeating: "Have to get home, have to get home"...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Hearing these words over and over reminded me of how long it was since I'd been back home myself. I'd be lying if I said a pang of homesickness didn't play a part in making me want to help him.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And so it was that I put my plans on hold. The Rainbough could wait. I made up my mind then and there to get the lad back to his village far away.\par
\par
\par
\lquote At the first inn we stayed at, we met a doctor from the desert who, as luck would have it, was heading the same way. No road is long with good company, as they say, so we decided to journey onward together.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2614\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a tourist pamphlet called \lquote The Rough Planet Guide to Sniflheim\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Though the individual snowflake is a tiny, beautiful crystal lighter than sparrow's down, the snowdrift is a vast and crushing mass of ice.\par
\par
\par
