An amazing coin I spied\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
Wondrous workmanship!\par
\par
\par
\lquote I made enquiries,\par
\par
Spent all day and learned its name:\par
\par
The mini medal.\par
\par
\par
\lquote I must leave Hotto\par
\par
And find the coin's creator,\par
\par
Learn how it was made.\par
\par
\lquote Do not fear, mother\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
I shall return a hero!\par
\par
A smith without peer!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh6098\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a picture book entitled \lquote The Tale of Miko and Ryu\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Brave Miko and Ryu,\par
\par
Protectors of the village,\par
\par
Scourge of the monsters.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Foul creatures attacked\par
\par
In numbers beyond counting,\par
\par
They drove them all back.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Yet there was one beast\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
The dragon of the mountain\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
They could not suppress.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But at last, success.\par
\par
The dragon was defeated,\par
\par
Though at what a cost...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Ryu was lost to us.\par
\par
Slain by foul Tatsunaga.\par
\par
Never forget him.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient diary that seems to have been written by a High Priestess of old. <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
But there's nothing of interest inside. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3775\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient diary that seems to have been written by a High Priestess of old. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Hotto's fortune grew.\par
\par
Great piles of shining treasure,\par
\par
Tall as Mount Huji.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Our stores overflowed,\par
\par
The glimmer lit the night sky,\par
\par
The surplus was moved.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Great treasures, Bloodstone,\par
\par
Look down upon the peak's fire,\par
\par
Reached by the back path...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Noah's Art\rquote . <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Almost anyone who's spent time among the less reputable people of Erdrea is bound to have heard of Noah, a man who trades in gossip and information of all kinds.\par
\par
\par
\lquote From the name of the local barber's mistress to the deepest, darkest secrets of the royal family, he knows every titbit of tattle and every scrap of scandal on every single street corner in the land.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But how does this mysterious figure come into possession of all these sensitive secrets? Many an intrepid investigator has tried to uncover his sources, but each and every one of them has failed.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But one thing is certain\f1\emdash\f0 his sense for a scoop is the stuff of legend. Some even say that on the day he was born, he pointed to the eastern sky, and that hours later, a storm rolled in from just that direction!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a picture book called \lquote Somewhere Under the Rainbow\rquote . <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Once upon a time, on a lovely summer's day, a rainbow appeared in the sky. The weather was so warm and relaxing that it made the rainbow sleepy, and he let out a great big yawn.\par
\par
\par
\lquote As he yawned, a single tear fell out of the corner of his eye, and the sparkling sunlight split it into seven different coloured lights, from which little baby lamplings were born!\par
\par
\par
\lquote The leafy lampling with his bright green cap of leaves, the luminous lampling with his brilliant blue flame, the lurid lampling with his shining yellow body...\par
\par
\par
\lquote But the red light was jealous of his beautiful brothers, so he gobbled the orange and violet lights up whole!\par
\par
\par
\lquote As punishment for this terrible sin, he was turned into the lava lampling. Horns grew from his head, and he was banished to hell, where he dwells to this day.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Doge Rotondo: The Best in the Business\rquote . <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Only a few short years ago, Gondolia was little more than a sleepy port town, but in the course of less than a decade, it has been transformed into what most agree is now the trade capital of Erdrea.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And who was it who brought about this stunning and sudden change? None other than Doge Rotondo, the current mayor. He attributes his success to avoiding one common pitfall: the fear of failure.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Business stops for nothing as far as this pioneer of profiteering is concerned\f1\emdash\f0 neither the fiercest of storms nor the most virulent of onboard plagues will convince him to stop a ship from sailing.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And this never-say-die attitude has paid off handsomely\f1\emdash\f0 the countless cargos that flow through the port every minute of the waking day are a testament to his fierce tenacity.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Viva Signor Universo!\rquote . <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote As proud citizens of the city of Gondolia, we must show to the world the most wonderful example of ourselves that is possible. And for our inspiration, we look to none other than the sea which surrounds us!\par
\par
\par
\lquote We must be as strong as the waves that buffet the ships in a storm, and as gentle as the breeze which fills the sails!\par
\par
\par
\lquote And what better way could there be to show the best of what our Gondolian men have to offer than the magnificent, fiery, feisty and fabulous Signor Universo contest!\par
\par
\par
\lquote So I say to all you salty, sweaty, strong young men: aim for the top! Be the best that you can be! And make Gondolia proud!\par
\par
\f1\emdash\f0  Doge Rotondo, First-Ever Signor Universo Winner\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh7550\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Diary of Tetsu the Smith\rquote . <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Part Two: A Dream Is Chased\par
\par
\par
\lquote My name is Tetsu.\par
\par
I am forty-eight years old.\par
\par
I am a blacksmith.\par
\par
\par
\lquote In Gondolia,\par
\par
A clue to the medal's source\par
\par
From a strapping man.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Far beyond the sea,\par
\par
A school for medal hunters\par
\par
Lies in a valley.\par
\par
\par
\lquote He says that this place\par
\par
Teaches the medals' secrets.\par
\par
I must learn them too.\par
\par
\par
\lquote A return to school\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
Funny perhaps at my age,\par
\par
But this is my dream.\par
\par
\lquote Do not fear, mother.\par
\par
I will become a great smith,\par
\par
And return home soon...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3775\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Memoirs of a Treasure Hunter: Volume I\rquote . <cc> takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote This journal tells the tale of the adventures of a humble treasure hunter. I hope that it might prove at least an amusing diversion for those who choose to read it.\par
\par
\par
\lquote My name is of little consequence, but if you must call me something, call me Sudo Nim.\par
\par
\par
\lquote So, what prompted me to set out on my quest? Well, the Zwaardsrustian Chief Minister's offer of one million gold coins for a certain artefact played no small part in my decision.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Legend has it that hundreds of years ago, when the Luminary returned from Yggdrasil, he brought something back with him: the Rainbough.\par
\par
\par
\lquote When I heard that this little stick could make me a millionaire, I didn't even take the time to pack\f1\emdash\f0 I was on the road in a flash!\par
\par
\par
\lquote And so began the adventurers of Sudo Nim, treasure hunter, and the quest for the elusive Rainbough...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3775\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a brochure called \lquote The 125th All-Erdrean Masked Martial Arts Tournament\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Welcome to the latest, and without a doubt the greatest, Masked Martial Arts tournament! Here's a sneak peek at just a few of the teams that'll be stepping into the ring this season for their shot at glory!\par
\par
\par
\lquote The Underdigger and the Abominable Showman: These muscle-bound heavyweights are ready to come down like a ton of king slimes on any opponent foolish enough to face them!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Liu Za, the Flying Dragon of Angri-La, and Golden Boy, the King of Charisma: They may look nothing alike, but these two brothers in justice make a killer combination!\par
\par
\par
\lquote The Beaty Queens, Sinderella and Whambelina: This delicious duo need no introduction\f1\emdash\f0 their looks alone are the stuff of legend, and their combat skills are just as sweet!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Who will emerge victorious? Who will lift the crown? There's only one way to find out, folks\f1\emdash\f0 come on down!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh5227\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Diary of Tetsu the Smith\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Chapter Three: A Dream Dies\par
\par
\par
\lquote My name is Tetsu.\par
\par
I am forty-eight years old.\par
\par
I am a blacksmith.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Black disappointment.\par
\par
The medal school forbids men\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
It is a girls' school.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The guard at the gate\par
\par
Bars the path to instruction,\par
\par
And so dies my dream...\par
\par
\lquote Wait for me, mother.\par
\par
Though I am not a great smith,\par
\par
I bring sweet flowers!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Chivalric Ideal\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Chivalry. All who dare to call themselves knights cherish this above all else. It is the criterion by which our worth is weighed.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Do not shirk in your duties or your training. Strive to exceed your limitations, be they physical or mental. At all times, and whoever you may encounter, be well-mannered and gentle.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But more sacred than any of these instructions is this: should you set yourself a goal, should you make a promise, do not fail to achieve it. Do not allow yourself to be swayed from your path.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Never\f1\emdash\f0 never\f1\emdash\f0 go back on your word. He who does so cannot claim to be any kind of knight. Take this firmly to heart, lest all your years of training be in vain.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl It looks like somebody's diary. Eleven takes it from the shelf and opens it at random...\par
\par
\par
\lquote At today's tournament, Se\'f1orito Norberto defeated Se\'f1or Hendrik! Words can scarcely express how thrilled I was to see such a display! He has grown mighty indeed!\rquote\par
\par
\par
Eleven skips forward several days...\par
\par
\lquote Se\'f1orito Norberto left today. I wish he would have at least said something before disappearing like that...\rquote\par
\par
\par
Eleven skips forward yet further still...\par
\par
\lquote A year has passed now since Se\'f1orito Norberto's departure, and still we hear nothing. I pray that he is safe...\rquote\par
\par
\par
The rest of the diary seems to be filled with similar entries. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh5227\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Diary of Tetsu the Smith\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Chapter Three: A Dream Dies\par
\par
\par
\lquote My name is Tetsu.\par
\par
I am forty-eight years old.\par
\par
I am a blacksmith.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Black disappointment.\par
\par
The medal school forbids men\f1\emdash\f0\par
\par
It is a girls' school.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The guard at the gate\par
\par
Bars the path to instruction,\par
\par
And so dies my dream...\par
\par
\lquote Wait for me, mother.\par
\par
Though I am not a great smith,\par
\par
I bring sweet flowers!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4356\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Memoirs of a Treasure Hunter: Volume II\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote This is the journal of Sudo Nim, treasure hunter extraordinaire. I came to this village after catching wind of a rumour that a schooner carrying the Rainbough was wrecked somewhere in Erdrea's southern seas.\par
\par
\par
\lquote In exchange for a couple of my best maps and charts, I enlisted the aid of the finest fisherman here. We dredged near enough the whole blessed ocean, but all we came back with was a few tasty scallops for tea.\par
\par
\par
\lquote So I've been spending a quiet evening in the bar enjoying our tasty catch, the village's local brew and the company of the landlord's beautiful daughter.\par
\par
\par
\lquote She tells me that my friend the fisherman is engaged to be married. He doesn't seem too keen on the arrangement, though. I shouldn't be surprised if he turned out to have his eye on someone else...\par
\par
\par
\lquote But it's late now and growing dark. I may not have found the Rainbough, but I've had a lovely day, and met some even lovelier people. Ahh, the traveller's life suits me down to the ground!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Dave: Legend\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Despite his humble beginnings as a farmer's son, our hero's winning personality and superior physical strength enabled him to quickly climb the ranks of the Zwaardsrustian Royal Navy.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But when his beloved king fell, he became a pink-masked privateer, striking fear into the hearts of the vilest scum of the seas, and expressing his grief in an incident that soon became infamous the world over.\par
\par
\par
\lquote With the help of a mysterious travelling entertainer friend, he somehow managed to paint the mast of every ship in the inland sea\f1\emdash\f0 frigates, freighters, clippers and caravels\f1\emdash\f0 a shocking shade of pink.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Even to this day, that bold and brilliant gesture is burnt into the memories of seafarers everywhere, and the name \ldblquote Dave\rdblquote  into the hearts and minds of admirers everywhere.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a large illustrated encyclopaedia entitled \lquote The Deadly Denizens of the Deep\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote The Fourth Deadly Denizen: Mermaids\par
\par
Mermaids are easily recognised, their upper halves taking the forms of human women, and their lower halves those of fish.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Their voices are prodigiously beautiful, and many a man has been sent peacefully to sleep by their dulcet tones, only to be dragged down through the inky depths to have his soul devoured.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Should you ever spy a beautiful woman in the water while at sea, do not call out to her, no matter how tempted you may be.\par
\par
\par
\lquote For she is almost certainly a mermaid, and will want nothing more than to sing you sweetly to sleep\f1\emdash\f0 a sleep from which you will never awaken.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh5808\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a hand-drawn book entitled \lquote Living With Me Under The Sea\rquote  with \lquote To Kai, my guy, from Michelle, your belle.\rquote  written on it. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Oh Kai, I just can't wait to live with you beneath the sea!\par
\par
A few rules just to help you settle in more easily:\par
\par
\par
\lquote First, don't panic\f1\emdash\f0 take it slowly, breathe a nice deep breath,\par
\par
Panicking while swimming is a recipe for death!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Next, no teasing\f1\emdash\f0 just because a fish looks small and meek,\par
\par
His mum might be ten times your size, then you'll be up the creek!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Third, don't look up\f1\emdash\f0 I'm not sure if you've seen how water flows,\par
\par
But waves can often send the current right up in your nose!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Fourth, clean your gills\f1\emdash\f0 they're like your lungs, try not to get them blocked,\par
\par
A bit of grit and you'll be in for quite the nasty shock!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Last but not least, think of others\f1\emdash\f0 selfishness is wrong!\par
\par
It's obvious I know, but it'll help you get along!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Astonishing Inventions of Gismo Mec\'e1nico\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Among the many fabulous creations left behind by the renowned engineer Gismo Mec\'e1nico, perhaps the best known is the stunning ship known as the Salty Stallion.\par
\par
\par
\lquote No other vessel in Erdrea can match this incredible craft in terms of beauty and speed, a quality experts tell us is imparted by its uniquely shaped prow.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Most boats are designed to cut through the water like a knife, but the Salty Stallion weaves through it instead like a needle through silk, leaving barely a wake behind it as it dances across the waves.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Its motion recalls that of the very man who commissioned it\f1\emdash\f0 a renowned entertainer and close personal friend of the ship's designer.\rquote  \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4066\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Wat Really Happened: The Destruction of Nhou Wat Explained\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote The events leading to the fall of the kingdom that stood on the site of Nhou Wat remain shrouded in mystery, but thanks to recent research on the topic, some details have finally come to light.\par
\par
\par
\lquote In nations whose populations die out gradually, tombs and grave sites are left behind as the survivors lay their dead to rest.\par
\par
\par
\lquote However, no signs remain of any tombs, crypts or even mass graves dating from the period of this particular civilisation's collapse.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Which would seem to suggest that whatever happened here happened quickly enough that no one remained to bury the dead.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Two other ruined kingdoms have followed the same distinctive pattern: the once-great nations of Zwaardsrust and Dundrasil.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Could the same fate that befell those two realms also have befallen the civilisation of old Nhou Wat\f1\emdash\f0 to wit, sudden and catastrophic monster attack?\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4356\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Memoirs of a Treasure Hunter: Volume III\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote This is the journal of Sudo Nim, treasure hunter extraordinaire. After hearing a rumour that the Rainbough was being offered as a prize in exchange for ninety-nine mini medals, I hurried to this school.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Of course, I should have known it was too good to be true. The prize on offer was nothing more than a Drasilian soldier's uniform (in a fetching shade of navy, mind you).\par
\par
\par
\lquote A rugged, practical outfit like that would be perfect for most adventurers, but it was a touch too tight around the belly for me, which made the sting of disappointment all the sharper.\par
\par
\par
\lquote My journey wasn't a complete waste, however\f1\emdash\f0 the fine young ladies of the academy told me of the kingdom of Sniflheim, where some of the most knowledgeable minds in all of Erdrea congregate.\par
\par
\par
\lquote If anywhere holds a clue as to the whereabouts of this accursed Rainbough, it'll be Sniflheim. I'm eager to head out, but first I'll need to find somewhere to spend the night. I can't spend it here...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a picture book entitled \lquote Wish Upon My Star\rquote . On the cover is a picture of a woman lying in bed, stroking a young boy's hair. Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote My dear Nisay, don't cry. Mama will not disappear forever.\par
\par
\par
\lquote I will ask Yggdrasil to make me a star, and place me high up in the sky.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And whenever you are sad or lonely\f1\emdash\f0 and even when you are happy\f1\emdash\f0 you can look up and see me watching over you.\par
\par
\par
\lquote So, my dear Nisay, don't cry. Keep your eyes dry so you can turn them upward and find Mama.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4356\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a tourist pamphlet called \lquote The Rough Planet Guide to Phnom Nonh\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Since its discovery deep within the ruins, the beautiful, smiling mural of Nhou Wat has gained something of a reputation for blessing visitors with good fortune, drawing sightseers from across the world.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The ruins themselves are thought to be all that remains of a once-powerful civilisation that was destroyed under mysterious circumstances hundreds of years ago.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But what could have spelled the end for so large a kingdom, blessed with such natural riches, and nestled within the safety of the mountain valleys? This is an enigma that has long troubled historians.\par
\par
\par
\lquote A king gone mad, driving his own legacy to ruin? An unforeseen and unprecedented natural disaster? A concentrated and cataclysmic attack by monsters? Hypotheses abound, but the mystery remains unsolved.\par
\par
\par
\lquote When you pay a visit to Nhou Wat, be sure to visit the mural and enjoy the blessings it gives, but spare a thought too for this once-great kingdom, and the tragic loss those ruins represent...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Don't Go Hungri: The Local Delicacies of Angri-La\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote It's widely agreed that Angri-La's unique style of cooking grew out of the need to provide delicious nutrition for the monks to perform their gruelling training while still adhering to a strict vegetarian diet.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Perhaps the temple's most famous dish is the legendary Bam Bam Noodles, which are served only at special festivals. Claims that this is the most delicious food in all the world are certainly not unfounded.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The meal is said to symbolise pride in one's achievements, and anyone capable of making the arduous mountain climb in order to taste them first-hand has every reason to be pleased with themselves!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book of wisdom entitled \lquote The Sutra of Angri-La\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote The master teaches that man is the world, and the world is man.\par
\par
To devote oneself to good deeds is to serve the world.\par
\par
To bring goodness into the world is to protect it.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The master teaches that through suffering, we learn of ease.\par
\par
That through sadness, we learn of joy.\par
\par
To love mankind and thereby the world\f1\emdash\f0 this is our duty.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Man is the world, goodness serves the world, learn good things from bad, and thereby love the world. These are the wisdoms of Angri-La, realm beyond the clouds. These are the precepts by which we live.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote On the Nature of the Naughty Stick\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote The grand masters of Angri-La wield a mighty weapon whose name echoes through the ages. I speak not of the Wavecutter Scimitar, nor of the Staff of Torn Clouds\f1\emdash\f0 no, I speak of the Naughty Stick.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The origins of this legendary tool of instruction can be traced back to the very founding of Angri-La. It is said that the Stick itself chose the very first grand master.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Some believe that it was carved from a branch of Yggdrasil, and that even a dragon could not break it, though it tried with all its might.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Of course, it is best known for its use in punishing young monks for lapses of focus. The pain it inflicts is rumoured to be so severe that acolytes fear that their very souls have been spanked from their bodies.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3775\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a tourist pamphlet entitled \lquote Girl About Town: Puerto Valor\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Start your day with a lazy morning relaxing by the water, and enjoy a traditional breakfast of pancakes with coconut sauce and strong Valorian coffee.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Then make your way to the beach, where you can sun yourself while enjoying a good book and snacking on delicious tropical fruit. The sweet, juicy flavours of fresh Valorian produce simply can't be beaten!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Once the day starts to cool, make your way to the casino and try your luck at the tables until it's time for dinner at the hotel's world-class restaurant. The chef's special is out of this world!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Finally, sit at the bar on the beachside terrace, sipping a cocktail and losing yourself in the stunning saffron sunset\f1\emdash\f0 or the bartender's arresting azure eyes...\par
\par
\par
\lquote This is just one of the many ways to while away a day in delectable Puerto Valor. If it sounds like your idea of fun, then don't delay\f1\emdash\f0 start planning your trip today!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh6389\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Memoirs of a Treasure Hunter: Volume V\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote This is the journal of Sudo Nim, treasure hunter extraordinaire. As it turns out, the young man I found collapsed on the way to Sniflheim was the son of this village's high priest.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The lad's father was overjoyed to see him alive and well, and as a reward, he offered myself and the desert doctor a choice between two great treasures.\par
\par
\par
\lquote I could scarce believe my eyes when I saw the first\f1\emdash\f0 a beautiful branch that glowed with all the colours in the world...the Rainbough! The very thing I'd spent all this time looking for!\par
\par
\par
\lquote The other treasure was a small stone that glowed with a curious blue light. The High Priest told us it was a magical artefact that would open the Door of Departure\f1\emdash\f0 a portal leading to a whole new adventure.\par
\par
\par
\lquote I'm sure I needn't tell you that I reached for the Rainbough in an instant...but at the last moment, something stayed my hand. I thought back over all that I'd experienced on my travels, and I realised...\par
\par
\par
\lquote I realised that it wasn't the Rainbough I'd been looking for all this time\f1\emdash\f0 it was the joy of the journey itself!\par
\par
\par
\lquote So I took the little blue stone and popped it safely in the pocket of my old, worn coat. The doctor, naturally, took the Rainbough.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And so it was that my quest came to an end. But it was by no means the end of my adventures!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Perhaps in the course of my continuing travels we might meet, dear reader. Just in case we do, let me tell you my name\f1\emdash\f0 I'm Chalky, the world's greatest adventurer!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Architect of the Ancients\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Many have heard the legends of Arboria's great statue of the Sage having been built long ago by an itinerant architect who spent the better part of his life on this one single masterpiece.\par
\par
\par
\lquote What is less well known is that this statue was created as a counterpart to another\f1\emdash\f0 that of the Luminary, which stands in ancient Dundrasil.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Indeed, it would seem that the fates of these two great statues were as wedded to one another as those of their subjects.\par
\par
\lquote So, dear reader, should your travels ever take you to Dundrasil, be sure to pay your respects to mighty Erdwin. Who knows what benefits the blessing of both these great monuments might bring...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Birth of Arboria\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Long, long ago, when the Dark One first terrorised the lands of Erdrea, a hero came forth and, with the aid of his companions, set out on a quest to end the tyranny of evil.\par
\par
\par
\lquote That hero was the Luminary. As time went on, a great many followers flocked to His cause. Those followers congregated here, and thus, the village of Arboria was born.\par
\par
\par
\lquote When the Luminary's work was done at last, the village remained, standing as an eternal testament to the gratitude of the peoples of the world for His great sacrifice.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And in time, the Arborians came to be known by another name\f1\emdash\f0 that of the Keepers. This title speaks to their solemn determination to see the Luminary's story preserved, and passed on to the generations to come.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an ancient book entitled \lquote Keepers, Dreamers\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Not more than once every few hundred years or thereabouts, a child is born in Arboria to whom the gift of foresight is granted. A foresight found in dreams.\par
\par
\par
\lquote At night, visions come to the recipient of this gift\f1\emdash\f0 visions that tell of the future.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Over the centuries, these visions have saved countless souls from misfortune. However, scant little is known of the origins of this sacred power.\par
\par
\par
\lquote One tantalising theory posited by the scholars of old is that the gift was received from the ancient inhabitants of the land whereupon the village stands. Inhabitants who disappeared into the very skies...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2614\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote HISTORY OF ERDREA. HISTORY OF TIME\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote WE ARE WATCHERS. THIS IS LEGEND OF WATCHERS. LEGEND OF LAW OF TIME.\par
\par
\par
\lquote SPIRITS WEAVE TIME. SPIRITS BORN FROM ERDREA. SPIRITS OF LOST TIME.\par
\par
\par
\lquote LIGHT GOVERNS TIME. HOLY LIGHT. SPIRITS OF LOST TIME GUARD HOLY LIGHT.\par
\par
\par
\lquote LIGHT GLOWS BRIGHT. BURNS. EXPLODES. WHEN IT DOES, LOST THINGS RETURN. ETERNITY IS UNDONE.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2614\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a peculiar book entitled \lquote SKY FISH GUIDE\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote SKY FISH. NO LEGS. HAS SPINE. SEVERAL SPECIES.\par
\par
\par
\lquote FOUND IN SKY. NOT LIKE ANIMALS OF LAND. BREATHES THROUGH GILLS. SKIN RUBBERY. SKIN DAMP.\par
\par
\par
\lquote TEMPERATURE CHANGE HURTS THEM. WARM: SOFT. HOT: EVAPORATE. HARD TO STORE. HARD TO BREED.\par
\par
\par
\lquote BUT DELICIOUS. SWEET AND SURPRISING. GOOD FOR PUDDINGS. GOOD RAW.\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4356\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an old book of poetry entitled \lquote Songs of Erdrea\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Song Two: The Little People\par
\par
\par
\lquote Lo, from the World Tree's shoots did fall,\par
\par
The little folk who witnessed all,\par
\par
\par
\lquote And down did rain Yggdrasil's seeds,\par
\par
And plants, then beasts, then humans breed,\par
\par
\par
\lquote When all was wrought, wyrm's light in hand,\par
\par
They upward went, and left the land,\par
\par
\par
\lquote Since then, from heav'n, the Watchers gazed,\par
\par
Looked o'er us all, their name be praised.\rquote  \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3485\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote All that Glitters Is Soon Gone \f1\endash\f0  A Tale of Condors and Criminality, by Davide Attenville.\rquote\par
\par
\par
\lquote Deep in the eastern reaches of the Champs Sauvage, a secluded valley sits high in the mountains. The locals call it the Eerie Eyrie, for it is the nesting place of that most infernal of flying fiends\f1\emdash\f0 the elysium bird.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Like many of its smaller avian cousins, this bird shows a compulsive interest in objects that twinkle and glisten, and will roam far and wide in search of such treasures.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The most egregious example of this behaviour occurred quite recently, when a particularly aggressive individual attacked a nearby manor house.\par
\par
\par
\lquote The beast tore through the very roof of the building, and made away with a large silver orb\f1\emdash\f0 the most priceless heirloom of the noble family who dwelt there.\par
\par
\lquote The monster was thought to have taken the orb back to the Eyrie, but a party sent to recover it never returned. It seems likely that both they and the treasure they sought will never be seen again...\rquote  \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl It looks like the previous year's student register.\par
\par
\par
There's a list of all kinds of weird and wonderful names followed by a note saying that the register for the next school year will be compiled soon.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh5227\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl\lquote L'Acad\'e9mie de Notre Ma\'eetre des M\'e9dailles - Official Register\par
\par
\par
\lquote #1 Conchella, #2 Fleur, #3 Angelique, #4 Jarmima, #5 Madeleine, #6 Gertrude, #7 Tallulah, #8 Chantelle, #9 Yolande,\par
\par
\par
\lquote #10 Adriane, #11 Sharla, #12 Oozenie, #13 Honore, #14 Clo\'e9,\par
\par
#15 Cl\'e9o, #16 Scholastique, #17 Else, #18 Vivien,\par
\par
\par
\lquote #19 Blaise, #20 Coco, #21 Trinny, #22 Carina, #23 Bashtienne,\par
\par
#24 Livvie, #25 Healoise,\par
\par
\par
\lquote #26 Candida, #27 Alice, #28 Mica, #29 Zazie, #30 Malodorine,\par
\par
#31 Purscilla\par
\par
\par
\lquote Teaching staff: Mme Waloppe, Mme Ch\'e9rie, Mme Labouche,\par
\par
Mme Augustine, Mlle Refaire, S\f2\u339?ur \f0\'c9sp\'e9e.\par
\par
Other Staff: M. Gardinier, Groundsman. Mme Croque, Chef.\par
\par
\par
\lquote This list is certified complete and correct by M. Maxime M\'e9daill\'e9, 11\'e8me Principal de l'Acad\'e9mie de Notre Ma\'eetre des M\'e9dailles.\rquote  \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh3194\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's an old book entitled \lquote The Medal-Winning Wisdom of Lady Minette Maximilien\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Mes ch\'e9ries, if ever you are lost as to how to be perfect little ladies, I ask you to do one thing for me\f1\emdash\f0 remember the example of the mini medal hunt.\par
\par
\par
\lquote What is the first thing we do when we set out in search of our little friends? That's right\f1\emdash\f0 we unroll our trusty world maps and think carefully about where we will begin our search.\par
\par
\par
\lquote In other words, we exercise our knowledge of the world and our powers of reason. It is these two things on which all our actions as mature, thoughtful ladies must be based.\par
\par
\par
\lquote To discover mini medals is to discover the world. And this is why we seek them out\f1\emdash\f0 because to be a woman in this day and age means to be a thinker and a doer par excellence!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Perfect Picnics for Monster-Riding Mademoiselles\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote A skullrider's steed is fast and strong, but not so fast that the rider's tummy doesn't start to rumble before he reaches his destination. Anyone who's travelled on monsterback knows that it's hungry work.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Which is why, whenever I set out to see the world atop a monster mount, I make sure to pack a hearty lunch.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Two large rounds of sandwiches and a pot of coffee with three lumps of sugar and plenty of milk\f1\emdash\f0 the perfect traveller's picnic!\par
\par
\par
\lquote With that in my knapsack, I'm ready to sit back and watch the world go by in style, knowing that I have a real treat awaiting me when hunger strikes!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl Eleven opens the book at random and sees the word \lquote JACKPOT!\rquote  printed in large letters on the page. It must be his lucky day!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh2904\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote The Seven Wonders of L'Acad\'e9mie de Notre Ma\'eetre des M\'e9dailles\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Wonder Number Seven: The mysterious Rose of the Window, a student slain in a terrible accident.\par
\par
\par
\lquote This spirit, once a pupil of l'Acad\'e9mie, is doomed not only to remain in our world, but to remain in the very spot where she met with her untimely death.\par
\par
\par
\lquote She appears in the prep rooms at night, and is never seen anywhere else. Her mournful face can be seen staring from the windows on cold and lonely evenings. At what she gazes, only she can know...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Perhaps she still dreams of graduating\f1\emdash\f0 something she can never do\f1\emdash\f0 and of the chance to go out and see the big, wide world...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4066\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote King Charlemini's Maximally Marvellous Idea\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Since long before the Medal King ever became a king, he lived only for his beloved mini medals. Gathering as many of his little golden friends as he could was all he ever cared about.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But the moment he held his newborn daughter in his arms, something changed. Suddenly he found himself caring about someone else's happiness. He wanted the best for his little girl, no matter what it took.\par
\par
\par
\lquote For three days and three nights, he racked his brains, trying to think how he might ensure that the princess grew to be a wise, graceful, beautiful woman who loved mini medals just as much as he did.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Then, on the morning of the fourth day, as he performed his daily exercises (specially tailored to help him seek out mini medals, of course), he had an idea.\par
\par
\par
\lquote\ldblquote Eureka!\rdblquote  he shouted. \ldblquote I shall create a school where young ladies can learn of the wonders of mini medals!\rdblquote  And so, l'Acad\'e9mie de Notre Ma\'eetre des M\'e9dailles was born!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4066\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Jolly Songs for Jolly Girls\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote\ldblquote Grubby, Grubby Grublins\rdblquote\par
\par
(A Traditional Zwaardsrustian Folk Song)\par
\par
Don't be shy\f1\emdash\f0 sing along!\par
\par
\par
\lquote Grubby, grubby grubliiins, so small and strange and lumpy! \f3\u9834?\f0\par
\par
Grubby, grubby grubliiins, some are gloomy, some are grumpy! \f3\u9834?\f0\par
\par
\par
\lquote Gloomy grublins\f1\emdash\f0 always sad! \f3\u9834?\f0\par
\par
Grumpy grublins\f1\emdash\f0 always mad! \f3\u9834?\f0\par
\par
Come on little grublins, oh it's not so bad! \f3\u9834?\f0\par
\par
\par
\lquote Grubby, grubby, grubby, grubby, grubby grubliiins! \f3\u9834?\rquote\f0\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4356\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a story entitled \lquote I Love to Hate You: A Schoolyard Scandal\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Standing in the unkempt field behind the school, the wind playing with the crimson scarf wrapped tightly around her neck and tousling her auburn hair, Emily's eyes burned with barely concealed rage.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Finally, Matilda appeared. The two girls locked eyes. The stalk of an unripe cherry poked from the corner of Matilda's mouth. \ldblquote You took your time, Emily!\rdblquote  Her voice was harsh, almost screaming.\par
\par
\par
\lquote\ldblquote Don't speak with your mouth full, Matilda,\rdblquote  Emily snapped back, \ldblquote You know how I hate that! You wouldn't want to make me angry now, would you?\rdblquote\par
\par
\par
\lquote Matilda grinned her wicked grin and spat the cherry pip high into the air, where it soared in a lazy arc.\par
\par
\par
\lquote And it was then that Emily realised: the moment the pip hit the ground would mark the start of the fateful final fight between these two long-standing rivals.\par
\par
\par
\lquote ...To be continued! Will Emily survive!? What will happen to Matilda!? Read the stunning conclusion in next month's issue: The Scarlet Scarf's Farewell!\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4066\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called \lquote Zwaardsrust: A Ruined Realm\rquote . Eleven takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote The lost kingdom of Zwaardsrust was ruled by the young king Arnout\f1\emdash\f0 a man so brave and noble that his subjects called him the Golden Lion.\par
\par
\par
\lquote King Arnout was beloved by his people, and he loved them fiercely in return. He formed an order of knights\f1\emdash\f0 paragons of strength and skill to a man\f1\emdash\f0 to protect his citizens and his borders.\par
\par
\par
\lquote But his glorious reign was cut tragically short. The monsters descended violently and without warning. The knights charged out to meet them with Arnout at their head...\par
\par
\par
\lquote Alas, their heroic efforts were in vain, and Zwaardsrust fell. Some say the monsters had come to fear the nation's growing army, prompting them to attack with ferocious force, but the truth remains a mystery.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Now little remains of that once-great kingdom save crumbling ruins. At night, the wind blowing through them sounds eerily like the mournful weeping of the slain king. A grim reminder of his tragic fate...\rquote\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh4937\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx10331 
\pard\intbl There's a book called the \lquote Lovey-Dovey Diaries\rquote . Jade takes it from the shelf and has a closer look...\par
\par
\par
\lquote My dearest, darling, super-smashing Boo! \f3\u9829?\f0  I've been thinking about you, and now my heart's beating so fast, I think I'm going to explode like a love volcano!\par
\par
\par
\lquote When are you going to wrap me up in those big, strong arms of yours? Tell me it'll be soon\f1\emdash\f0 I've already waited far, far, far too long!\par
\par
Yours forever and ever, Boodica \f3\u9829?\f0  \f3\u9829?\f0  \f3\u9829?\rquote\f0\par
\par
\par
\lquote My darling! My precious! My Boodica! How I have missed your all-conquering curves! One day soon, I'll sweep you off your feet, just as I've always promised!\par
\par
\par
\lquote But my sweet, you will have to wait a little longer. We must do things correctly. First we'll use these pages to get to know each other, then I'll ask the Lord of Shadows to officially approve our union.\par
\par
\par
\lquote Then, on the tenth anniversary of our first date, we'll sit together under a starry sky and\f1\emdash\f0 oh, my pen quivers as I write this!\f1\emdash\f0 hold hands for the very first time!\par
\par
\lquote Can you imagine, my dearest? Can you? Hold onto that thought\f1\emdash\f0 treasure it until the day comes at long last!\par
\par
Yours in anticipation, Booga \f3\u9829?\f0  \f3\u9829?\f0  \f3\u9829?\rquote\f0\par
\par
\par
The book contains hundreds more of Booga and Boodica's sickeningly saccharine love letters. Jade pops it back on the shelf with a shudder.\cell\row 
